    "summary": "“The seasonal spread tightening is in full swing, with an average market yield of 5.05% as of end of August.” Further noting that, “The market yield has now reached 2020 levels, highlighting one more time the softening of the market.” Click the chart below to analyse the interactive data : It’s worth noting that a year ago the overall coupon of the catastrophe bond market according to this data set stood at 10.22%, some 13% higher that today. During August 2026 catastrophe bond seasonal spread tightening accelerated and as a result the catastrophe bond market yield , or coupon available to investors, fell around 4.5% in the month. Which leaves it now 13% lower than it was at the same time last year, according to the latest data on cat bond yields from Plenum Investments.",
