    "title": "Cyber reinsurance market to shift focus to strategic deployment: Ariel Re’s Carr",
    "title_original": "Cyber reinsurance market to shift focus to strategic deployment: Ariel Re’s Carr",
    "url": "https://www.reinsurancene.ws/cyber-reinsurance-market-to-shift-focus-to-strategic-deployment-ariel-res-carr/",
    "summary": "Ample capacity and sustained competitive pricing will characterise the cyber reinsurance market, but the core discussion is shifting from sheer volume to strategic deployment, Daniel Carr, Head of Cyber Underwriting at Ariel Re, stated in a recent interview with Reinsurance News. We expect the discussion to move beyond simply how much cyber reinsurance is available towards how cedents allocate that capacity across the loss distribution.” This reassessment is driving a shift in buyer behaviour ahead of the January 1, 2027, renewals, where Carr anticipates a “more deliberate approach” centred on structure, attachment, and event definition rather than a dramatic pricing shift. According to Carr, as the reinsurance industry meets at Rendez-Vous de Septembre (RVS) 2026 in Monte Carlo, the question for the market is no longer how much capacity exists, but where along the loss distribution cedents choose to deploy it.",
