    "url": "https://www.reinsurancene.ws/ms-res-bruniecki-says-retentions-to-hold-as-attachment-points-stay-disciplined/",
    "summary": "Especially, as casualty is such a diverse universe where risks are big and very volatile, I do think risk and rating go more hand in hand.” Turning to terms and conditions, and specifically attachment points, Bruniecki argued that discipline throughout the risk chain is what has kept retentions intact since the market reset of 2022. People will have to get disciplined in their underwriting because we cannot support business which is below technically adequate levels.” Casualty, in Bruniecki’s assessment, remains a different story, with rate adequacy still an open question given how varied the class of business is. I do think for the most part retentions will stay in place.",
