  {
    "id": "swiss-re-expects-to-remain-a-meaningful-participant-in-alternative-capital-baert",
    "title": "Swiss Re expects to remain a meaningful participant in alternative capital: Baertschi",
    "title_original": "Swiss Re expects to remain a meaningful participant in alternative capital: Baertschi",
    "url": "https://www.artemis.bm/news/swiss-re-expects-to-continue-being-a-meaningful-participant-in-alternative-capital-baertschi/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=swiss-re-expects-to-continue-being-a-meaningful-participant-in-alternative-capital-baertschi",
    "summary": "Speaking today at Swiss Re’s briefing at RVS 2026 in Monte Carlo, Urs Baertschi, Chief Executive Officer, of P&C Reinsurance, underscored the importance of the reinsurers third-party capital markets focused Alternative Capital Partners (ACP) division, and stated that Swiss Re expects to continue to be a “meaningful participant in that market.” During Swiss Re’s media briefing at RVS today, Baertschi stressed the overall importance of the reinsurance industry having a strong capital base. The rest we think of as alternative capital as well.” Baertschi continued: “Alternative capital is an important part of the capital stack, and the opportunities that insurance companies and buyers of this kind of protection have, and it also very importantly supports the traditional reinsurance capacity.” In light of this, we asked senior executives what the reinsurer’s plans were for growing its Alternative Capital Partners division into 2027. Earlier this year, Swiss Re launched a new Alternative Capital Solutions unit to encompass its activities in ILS and retrocessional hedging and execution.",
