    "summary": "Speaking during the firm’s briefing at the 2026 Rendez-Vous de Septembre (RVS) in Monte Carlo, Stefan Golling, a Member of the Board of Management of Munich Re, suggested that the industry has not done enough to close the significant cyber protection gap, while also flagging the major business opportunity in doing so as Munich Re looks to maintain its position as a market leader in the growing sector. He went on, “Closing the cyber protection gap is a major business opportunity, but it’s also our responsibility as an industry if we want to live up to the picture of being the immune system for our customers. Golling observed that much of the growth in cyber has come over the past 24 to 36 months and, with rates having softened, said he believes the industry has not done enough to close the significant protection gap.",
