  {
    "id": "ils-will-return-to-the-cyber-conversation-in-time-ai-risk-a-future-factor-baker-",
    "title": "ILS will return to the cyber conversation in time. AI risk a future factor: Baker, CyberCube",
    "title_original": "ILS will return to the cyber conversation in time. AI risk a future factor: Baker, CyberCube",
    "url": "https://www.artemis.bm/news/ils-will-return-to-the-cyber-conversation-in-time-ai-risk-a-future-factor-baker-cybercube/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=ils-will-return-to-the-cyber-conversation-in-time-ai-risk-a-future-factor-baker-cybercube",
    "summary": "Speaking with Artemis around the time of the Monte Carlo Reinsurance Rendez-vous event, Baker said that investor engagement on understanding cyber risk and readying themselves to invest in the cyber ILS asset class continues. Baker of CyberCube explained why the cyber cat bond market has been quiet of late, highlighting the economics, “The soft market means traditional reinsurance capacity exists at lower prices, which decreases the general need to reach towards the ILS market for risk and capital management. “On top of that, cyber balance sheets are not yet a significant driver in a lot of carrier or reinsurance companies’ overall risk, so time and resources get spent elsewhere first right now.” She continued to say that investor interest is not a limiting factor, “That said, from what we can see there is more investor demand than sponsor supply, so that’s not holding back the market at this time.",
