    "summary": "Anthony Cordonnier, Global Co-Head of Cyber, Managing Director at reinsurance broker Marsh Re, said a meaningful shift that is beginning to appear is a willingness among some buyers to explore higher cessions at the 1 January 2027 cyber renewals. In an interview with Reinsurance News around the annual meeting of the reinsurance industry in Monte Carlo, Cordonnier explained that buyers of cyber reinsurance are exploring higher cessions as they reassess whether their current programmes are appropriately sized for the risks they are running. At the key 1.1 2027 cyber renewals, Cordonnier noted that buyers with the widest range of options are likely to be those that have invested properly in understanding their exposure and can articulate a coherent underwriting strategy to the market.",
