    "title": "Capital inflows, low cat losses to pressure Jan 1 rates, structural integrity the focus in ILS: Twelve Securis",
    "title_original": "Capital inflows, low cat losses to pressure Jan 1 rates, structural integrity the focus in ILS: Twelve Securis",
    "url": "https://www.artemis.bm/news/capital-inflows-low-cat-losses-to-pressure-jan-1-rates-structural-integrity-the-focus-in-ils-twelve-securis/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=capital-inflows-low-cat-losses-to-pressure-jan-1-rates-structural-integrity-the-focus-in-ils-twelve-securis",
    "summary": "An influx of capital inflows and low catastrophe losses are likely to pressure rates at the upcoming January renewals, which leads Twelve Securis’ Cahal Doris to note that structural integrity will remain a key focus for the insurance-linked securities (ILS) market during the key season. All of which leads the CIO to note that structural integrity remains a key focus for ILS. In a market that is expected to soften absent any catastrophes, the managers that have access to a broad range of opportunities are best placed.” Sticking with the January renewals, Doris explained that he believes competitive pressure will likely remain a feature of the ILS market if catastrophe activity continues to remain manageable and capital also continues to be abundant.",
