    "summary": "The insurance-linked securities (ILS) market will see strong demand through the end of 2026 and into 2027, while the asset class is also likely to grow further with catastrophe bonds and sidecars key areas as cedents integrate ILS products into their reinsurance, according to Richard Pennay, CEO of Aon Securities. Facilitating these reinsurance partnership’s, Pennay said that Aon works with its clients to “ultimately form a view as to how ILS can complement those structures.” Pennay continued to explain, “In addition to that demand from our clients, we are seeing an overwhelming supply of capacity from the insurance-linked securities investors. “The ILS market today is truly at its strongest stance that it has ever been over the 20 plus year evolution of this market,” Pennay explained, “We certainly have the sense that that this market is at its strongest point today.",
