    "title": "Reinsurers maintain cautious approach to data centre accumulation risk: Arrivé, Fitch",
    "title_original": "Reinsurers maintain cautious approach to data centre accumulation risk: Arrivé, Fitch",
    "url": "https://www.reinsurancene.ws/reinsurers-maintain-cautious-approach-to-data-centre-accumulation-risk-arrive-fitch/",
    "summary": "Manuel Arrivé, Head of EMEA Reinsurance Ratings at Fitch Ratings, said the growth of data centres and digital infrastructure in general presents both an opportunity and significant risk for reinsurers due to potential exposure, accumulation risk and modelling challenges. During Fitch’s 2027 Global Reinsurance Outlook webinar, Arrivé noted that reinsurers tend to take a very cautious approach towards data centres. Arrivé continued, “But the main challenge and main risks for reinsurers is the accumulation risk, where one incident can trigger claims from different policies, different clients, and that has consequences also in terms of modelling.” Nevertheless, Arrivé highlighted the impressive scale of investment in data centres, with trillions of dollars expected to be invested in the sector in the coming years, creating a significant opportunity for the insurance and reinsurance industry.",
