    "summary": "The performance of insurance-linked securities investment fund strategies, across catastrophe bonds and private ILS, has continued to rise through July 2026 with the month delivering the best returns of the year so far for the asset class, as measured by the ILS Advisers Fund Index . This strong July average ILS fund return has lifted performance for the first seven months of 2026 to 5.12% for the Index. ILS Advisers said that, “Pure cat bond funds as a group posted a 0.95% gain for the month, while funds incorporating private ILS strategies were up by 1.23% on average.” The range of returns reported was also indicative of a very strong month for the ILS fund marketplace, as the worst performing fund delivered a 0.45% return and the best-performing a much stronger 2.88% for July 2026.",
